# .gitmodules
#
# This file links the students' submission repositories into this course
# repository as git submodules. Each student (or team) keeps their work in a
# separate repository created inside the iaac-maai GitHub organization (not on
# their personal profile); this repository only stores a pointer to a specific
# commit of it. This way students keep full control of their own history and
# branches, and no one needs write access to the course repository.
#
# Submissions live under:  Day_<N>/submissions/<student-name>
#                          hackathon/submissions/<team-name>
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Adding a submission (done by the course maintainers)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   git submodule add <repo-url> Day_<N>/submissions/<student-or-team-name>
#   git commit -m "Add submission: <student-or-team-name>"
#
# This command appends an entry to this file automatically, for example:
#
# [submodule "Day_1/submissions/<student-or-team-name>"]
#     path = Day_1/submissions/<student-or-team-name>
#     url = https://github.com/iaac-maai/<repo-name>.git
#     branch = main
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloning this repository with all submissions
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   git clone --recurse-submodules <this-repo-url>
#
# If you already cloned it without submissions:
#   git submodule update --init --recursive
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Updating submissions to their latest commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   git submodule update --remote --merge
#   git add Day_*/submissions hackathon/submissions
#   git commit -m "Update submissions"
#
# Notes for students:
#   - Create your repository inside the iaac-maai organization
#     (https://github.com/iaac-maai), not on your personal profile.
#     Repositories on personal profiles will not be linked.
#   - Push your final work to the branch listed above (default: main) before
#     the deadline. The course repository records the exact commit that was
#     submitted.
#   - Do not edit this file yourself; ask the course maintainers to add or
#     change your entry.
